Requirement Analysis Phase
# ComicCraft — Requirement Analysis Phase

 The **Requirement Analysis Phase** defines exactly what ComicCraft must do, who will use it, what the system needs to support, and what conditions must be satisfied before the project can be considered complete.

 # 1\. Project Identification

 **Project Name:** ComicCraft\
 **Project Type:** AI-powered web application\
 **Domain:** Artificial Intelligence / Creative Writing / Comic Creation\
 **Primary AI:** Gemini models\
 **Target Platform:** Web browser

 ### Project vision

 > **ComicCraft enables users to transform an idea into an editable comic story with the assistance of Gemini AI.**

---

 # 2\. Problem Analysis

 Creating a comic traditionally requires several separate activities:

```
Story Idea
    ↓
Story Writing
    ↓
Character Creation
    ↓
Storyboarding
    ↓
Panel Planning
    ↓
Dialogue Writing
    ↓
Artwork
    ↓
Layout
    ↓
Editing
```

 A beginner may have difficulty managing all these stages.

 ComicCraft combines the **storytelling and planning stages** into a single AI-assisted workflow.

---

 # 3\. Proposed Solution

 ComicCraft should provide a guided workflow:

```
User Idea
    ↓
Comic Creation Form
    ↓
Gemini AI
    ↓
Story
    ↓
Characters
    ↓
Pages
    ↓
Panels
    ↓
Dialogue
    ↓
Comic Editor
    ↓
Preview
    ↓
Export
```

 The user remains responsible for reviewing and editing the generated content.

---

