 # 5\. Target Users

 ComicCraft should support:

 - Students
- Comic enthusiasts
- Writers
- Beginner artists
- Content creators
- Teachers
- Parents
- Indie creators

 The interface should therefore be approachable for users without programming or AI experience.

---

 # 6\. Functional Requirements

 Functional requirements describe **what the system must do**.

 ## FR-01 — User Registration

 The system shall allow users to create an account.

 The registration process should collect appropriate account information and validate it.

---

 ## FR-02 — User Authentication

 The system shall allow registered users to:

 - Sign in
- Sign out
- Maintain a secure session

---

 ## FR-03 — Dashboard

 The system shall provide a dashboard containing:

 - Create Comic
- Recent Projects
- Saved Comics
- Project status
- Project management actions

---

 ## FR-04 — Create Comic Project

 Users shall be able to create a new project.

 The project should support:

 - Title
- Story idea
- Genre
- Art style
- Tone
- Number of pages
- Panels per page
- Language

---

 # 7\. Story Generation Requirements

 ## FR-05 — AI Story Generation

 ComicCraft shall use Gemini to generate a story from the user's input.

 The generated story should contain:

 - Title
- Summary
- Story structure
- Characters
- Pages
- Panels
- Dialogue
- Captions
- Scene descriptions

---

 ## FR-06 — Character Generation

 Gemini shall generate structured character information.

 Each character may contain:

```
Name
Age
Role
Description
Personality
Appearance
Strengths
Weaknesses
```

---

 ## FR-07 — Story Outline

 The system should generate a logical story progression:

```
Beginning
   ↓
Conflict
   ↓
Rising Action
   ↓
Climax
   ↓
Resolution
```

---

 # 8\. Comic Panel Requirements

 ## FR-08 — Page Generation

 The system shall divide the generated story into pages.

 Each page should have:

 - Page number
- Panels
- Story context

---

 ## FR-09 — Panel Generation

 Each page shall contain one or more panels.

 Each panel should support:

 - Scene description
- Visual prompt
- Caption
- Dialogue
- Characters involved

---

 ## FR-10 — Dialogue Generation

 The system shall generate dialogue appropriate to:

 - Character
- Scene
- Genre
- Tone
- Story context

---

 # 9\. Comic Editor Requirements

 ## FR-11 — Panel Editing

 Users shall be able to edit:

 - Scene descriptions
- Captions
- Dialogue
- Panel content

---

 ## FR-12 — Page Management

 Users shall be able to:

 - Add pages
- Delete pages
- Reorder pages
- Navigate between pages

---

 ## FR-13 — Panel Management

 Users shall be able to:

 - Add panels
- Delete panels
- Reorder panels
- Edit panels

---

 # 10\. AI-Assisted Editing Requirements

 ## FR-14 — Regenerate Panel

 Users shall be able to regenerate an individual panel.

 The rest of the comic should remain unchanged unless explicitly modified.

---

 ## FR-15 — Rewrite Dialogue

 Users shall be able to request alternative dialogue.

 Examples:

```
Make it funnier
Make it shorter
Make it more dramatic
Make it suitable for children
```

---

 ## FR-16 — Continue Story

 The system shall allow users to continue an existing story.

 Gemini should use relevant existing story context and character information when generating the continuation.

---

 ## FR-17 — Story Consistency

 ComicCraft should maintain a **Story Bible** containing important information such as:

 - Characters
- Locations
- World rules
- Timeline
- Tone
- Important objects

 This information should be used when performing subsequent AI operations.

---

 # 11\. Project Management Requirements

 ## FR-18 — Save Project

 Users shall be able to save their comics.

 Projects should persist after:

 - Browser refresh
- Logout
- Re-login

---

 ## FR-19 — Edit Existing Project

 Users shall be able to open a previously saved comic and continue editing it.

---

 ## FR-20 — Delete Project

 Users shall be able to delete projects they own.

 Deletion should be handled carefully to prevent accidental data loss.

---

 # 12\. Preview Requirements

 ## FR-21 — Comic Reader

 The system shall provide a dedicated preview mode.

 It should support:

 - Page navigation
- Previous/next page
- Full-screen reading
- Panel rendering
- Dialogue rendering
- Captions

---

 # 13\. Export Requirements

 ## FR-22 — Export Comic

 The system should allow users to export their comic.

 Initial formats:

 - PDF
- PNG/image

 The exported output should preserve page order and comic layout.

---

 # 14\. AI Requirements

 Gemini integration is a core requirement.

 ### AI operations

```
Gemini
│
├── Generate Story
├── Generate Characters
├── Generate Outline
├── Generate Pages
├── Generate Panels
├── Generate Dialogue
├── Rewrite Dialogue
├── Regenerate Panel
└── Continue Story
```

 AI responses should use a predictable structured format.

---

 # 15\. Structured Output Requirement

 ComicCraft should not rely exclusively on free-form text.

 Expected structure:

```
{
  "title": "Comic Title",
  "summary": "Story summary",
  "characters": [],
  "pages": [
    {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "panels": [
        {
          "panelNumber": 1,
          "sceneDescription": "...",
          "caption": "...",
          "dialogue": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

 The application should validate this data before displaying or storing it.

---

 # 16\. AI Error Requirements

 The application shall handle cases where:

 - Gemini is unavailable.
- The request times out.
- The response is malformed.
- The response does not conform to the expected schema.
- The generation request is rejected.
- The user exceeds usage limits.

 Example:

```
Unable to generate your comic right now.

Your existing work is safe.

[Try Again]
```

---

 # 17\. Non-Functional Requirements

 ## NFR-01 — Performance

 The application should provide responsive UI interactions.

 AI operations should display progress states rather than appearing frozen.

---

 ## NFR-02 — Security

 The application shall:

 - Protect API keys.
- Authenticate users.
- Authorize project access.
- Validate input.
- Validate AI output.
- Protect user data.

 The Gemini API key must never be exposed in client-side code.

---

 ## NFR-03 — Reliability

 The system should avoid losing user work when:

 - AI generation fails.
- Network connectivity is interrupted.
- Database operations fail.

---

 ## NFR-04 — Usability

 A new user should be able to create a basic comic without technical knowledge.

 The main workflow should be understandable:

 **Create → Generate → Edit → Preview → Export**

---

 ## NFR-05 — Scalability

 The architecture should allow future additions such as:

 - AI artwork
- Collaboration
- Public sharing
- Mobile applications
- Voice narration
- Animated comics

---

 ## NFR-06 — Maintainability

 The codebase should use:

 - Reusable components
- Modular AI services
- Centralized validation
- Clear API boundaries
- Consistent naming
- Version control

---

 # 18\. Security Requirements

 ### Authentication

 Only authenticated users should access private projects.

 ### Authorization

 Users can only modify their own projects.

 ### API protection

 AI endpoints should be protected against excessive requests.

 ### Secrets

 Environment variables should be used for:

```
GEMINI_API_KEY
DATABASE_URL
AUTH_SECRET
```

 ### Input validation

 Validate:

 - Story prompts
- Project IDs
- Page IDs
- Panel IDs
- User-generated text
- AI responses

