 # 25\. MVP Boundary

 The most important requirement decision is to keep the first release focused.

 ### Core MVP

```
       USER IDEA
           ↓
      GEMINI AI
           ↓
        STORY
           ↓
     CHARACTERS
           ↓
       PANELS
           ↓
        EDITOR
           ↓
       PREVIEW
           ↓
        EXPORT
```

 Advanced artwork generation should be treated as a separate capability rather than making it a dependency for the initial story-generation MVP.

---

 # 26\. Final Requirement Summary

 ComicCraft's requirements can be summarized into **five major functional areas**:

 | Area | Main Requirements |
| --- | --- |
| User Management | Registration, login, authorization |
| AI Creation | Story, characters, pages, panels, dialogue |
| Comic Editing | Edit, regenerate, rewrite, continue |
| Project Management | Save, load, update, delete |
| Output | Preview and export |

### Core requirement

 > **ComicCraft must allow a user to transform a simple idea into an editable, structured comic with the assistance of Gemini models, while keeping the user in control of the final content.**

 This requirement becomes the foundation for the **System Design → Development → Testing → Deployment** stages of the project.
